IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc8-part8-duties`

-- ccc8-tests-part8-duties.l4 -- tests for ccc8-part8-duties.l4 (sections 214 to 218). Expected values are written by hand from the text.
-- The stand-in below is NOT the penalty of section 787(1) (outside this part): it states nothing, so only the limb of this part is tested.
`s 215(3) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 214 -- definitions`

-- "abandon or expose includes (a) a wilful omission to take charge of a child by a person who is under a legal duty to do so, and (b) dealing with a child in a manner that is likely to leave that child exposed to risk without protection"
#ASSERT `s 214 abandon or expose` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 214 abandon or expose` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 214 abandon or expose` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "form of marriage includes a ceremony of marriage that is recognized as valid (a) by the law of the place where it was celebrated, or (b) by the law of the place where an accused is tried"
#ASSERT `s 214 form of marriage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 214 form of marriage` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 214 form of marriage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "guardian includes a person who has in law or in fact the custody or control of a child"
#ASSERT `s 214 guardian` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 214 guardian` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 214 guardian` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 215 -- necessaries of life`

-- (1)(a) "as a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family, to provide necessaries of life for a child under the age of sixteen years": age 15 is under, 16 is not
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(a) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` TRUE 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(a) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(a) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` TRUE 16 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(a) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` FALSE 5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b) "to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner"
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(b) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(b) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(b) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(b) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(c) "to a person under his charge if that person (i) is unable, by reason of detention, age, illness, mental disorder or other cause, to withdraw himself from that charge, and (ii) is unable to provide himself with necessaries of life"
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(c) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(c) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(c) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(1)(c) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "Every one is under a legal duty (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..."
#ASSERT `s 215(1) the person is under a legal duty` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(1) the person is under a legal duty` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(1) the person is under a legal duty` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(1) the person is under a legal duty` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the three duties as regulative rules: no time limit is stated; a trace with the act is fulfilled, one with nothing prints the standing duty
#TRACE `s 215(1)(a) the duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 215(1)(a) provide necessaries of life for the child` AT 5
#TRACE `s 215(1)(a) the duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` AT 0 WITH
#TRACE `s 215(1)(b) the duty to provide necessaries of life to the spouse or common-law partner` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 215(1)(b) provide necessaries of life to the spouse or common-law partner` AT 5
#TRACE `s 215(1)(c) the duty to provide necessaries of life to the person under the person's charge` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 215(1)(c) provide necessaries of life to the person under the person's charge` AT 5
-- (2) "Every person commits an offence who, being under a legal duty ..., fails without lawful excuse to perform that duty, if (a) with respect to a duty imposed by paragraph (1)(a) or (b), (i) the person to whom the duty is owed is in destitute or necessitous circumstances, or (ii) the failure ... endangers the life ... or ... health ... endangered permanently; or (b) with respect to a duty imposed by paragraph (1)(c), the failure ... endangers the life ... or ... health ... injured permanently"
--                                                                                         duty         (a)or(b) (c)   fails excuse destitute end(a/b) end(c)
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (JUST TRUE) TRUE  FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (JUST TRUE) TRUE  FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (JUST TRUE) TRUE  FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE  TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE  TRUE FALSE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (JUST TRUE) TRUE  FALSE TRUE TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (JUST TRUE) TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` NOTHING     TRUE  FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (JUST FALSE) TRUE  FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 215(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 215(3) the punishment` `s 215(3) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 215(3) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- (4)(b) "evidence that a person has in any way recognized a child as being his child is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the child is his child"
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(b) the recognition is proof that the child is his child` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(b) the recognition is proof that the child is his child` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(b) the recognition is proof that the child is his child` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4)(c) "evidence that a person has failed for a period of one month to make provision for the maintenance of any child of theirs under the age of sixteen years is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the person has failed without lawful excuse"
-- the failure begins on 15 January 2025: one month is complete on 15 February (the day before it is not)
--                                                                                                       from             as at            child  age  contrary
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` (Date 15 1 2025) (Date 14 2 2025) TRUE 15 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` (Date 15 1 2025) (Date 15 2 2025) TRUE 15 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` (Date 15 1 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE 15 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` (Date 15 1 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE 16 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` (Date 15 1 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE 5 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a failure from 31 January: a month later falls in a shorter month, and the month is complete on its last day (28 February 2025)
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 27 2 2025) TRUE 15 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 28 2 2025) TRUE 15 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4)(d) "the fact that a spouse or common-law partner or child is receiving or has received necessaries of life from another person who is not under a legal duty to provide them is not a defence"
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(d) the receipt of necessaries of life from another person is a defence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(d) the receipt of necessaries of life from another person is a defence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 215(4)(d) the receipt of necessaries of life from another person is a defence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 216 to 218`

-- 216 "Every one who undertakes to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person or to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person is, except in cases of necessity, under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care in so doing"
--                                                                                                                  medical other necessity
#ASSERT `s 216 the person is under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216 the person is under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216 the person is under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` TRUE  FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216 the person is under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` FALSE TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216 the person is under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216 the person is under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 216 the duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 216 have and use reasonable knowledge, skill and care in the treatment or act undertaken` AT 2
-- 217 "Every one who undertakes to do an act is under a legal duty to do it if an omission to do the act is or may be dangerous to life"
#ASSERT `s 217 the person is under a legal duty to do the act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 217 the person is under a legal duty to do the act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 217 the person is under a legal duty to do the act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 217 the duty to do the act undertaken` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 217 do the act undertaken` AT 2
-- 217.1 "Every one who undertakes, or has the authority, to direct how another person does work or performs a task is under a legal duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm"
#ASSERT `s 217.1 the person is under a legal duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 217.1 the person is under a legal duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 217.1 the duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 217.1 take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm arising from the work or task` AT 2
-- 218 "Every one who unlawfully abandons or exposes a child who is under the age of ten years, so that its life is or is likely to be endangered or its health is or is likely to be permanently injured, (a) ... not exceeding five years; or (b) summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 218 the person commits the offence of abandoning a child` TRUE 9 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 218 the person commits the offence of abandoning a child` TRUE 10 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 218 the person commits the offence of abandoning a child` TRUE 9 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 218 the person commits the offence of abandoning a child` FALSE 9 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 218 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 218 the punishment` `s 215(3) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 215(3) test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
